{title: Remain in My Love}
{subtitle: John 15:9–11}
{key: Db}
{tempo: 86}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [Db] | [Db] | [Db] | [Ab/C] |
| [Ab/C] | [Bbm7] | [Bbm7] | [Gb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
If you [Db]remain in me and my [Ab/C]words remain in you
Ask [Bbm7]whatever you wish and it [Gb]will be done for you
This is [Db]how my Father is glorified in your [Ab/C]life
[Bbm7]Bear much fruit and prove you are [Gb]my disciples
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
As [Bbm7]the Father has loved [Ab]me with a love so [Gb]true
So [Bbm7]I have loved you [Ab]as well in ev[Gb]ery view
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Re[Db]main in my love and let your [Ab/C]heart be still
Keep my [Bbm7]commandments and walk with me a [Gb]while
I [Db]have told you this so that my joy [Ab/C]may be in you
And your joy may be [Bbm7]complete and [Gb]new
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
If you [Db]keep my commandments you will re[Ab/C]main in my love
[Bbm7]Just as I have kept my Father's [Gb]commandments above
I [Db]remain in his love and [Ab/C]he remains in me
This is [Bbm7]the path that I freely [Gb]give to see
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
This [Db]is my commandment that you [Ab/C]love one another
[Bbm7]As I have loved you with[Gb]out end or another
[Db]No one has greater love than to [Ab/C]lay down his life
For [Bbm7]his friends who are called to [Gb]this holy life
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Db]You are my [Ab/C]friends if you [Bbm7]do what I com[Gb]mand
Re[Db]main in my love [Ab/C]and hold my [Bbm7]loving [Gb]hand
{end_of_verse}
